==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|basketball}} The achievement of a two-digit number of all five of points scored, assists, rebounds, blocks, and steals in a single game. There has never been an official quintuple double in NBA play.
#: ''In a 1968 regular season game vs the Los Angeles Lakers, Wilt Chamberlin finished with a recorded 53 points,  32 rebounds, 14 assists,    24 blocks and 12 steals. The NBA did not begin keeping official stats until 1972, however, so although Chamberlin may have finished with the only quintuple double in NBA history, it cannot be considered official NBA history.''

